    "result_text": "There's only one test class, and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the membership-level tenure rule in `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`.\n\n**Change to `getMembershipLevel()`:**\n- The pre-tenure factors (base 1, +1 for email, +1 for `namesakeCount == 0`) are now explicitly **capped at 3**.\n- A new **level-4 factor**: tenure of **more than 365 days**, measured as `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, LocalDate.now()) > 365`, adds one more level, with the final result capped at 4.\n- Since a newly created owner's `registrationDate` is today (zero tenure), the tenure factor never fires for new owners, so they max out at level 3 \u2014 matching the acceptance test (`coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3`), where an owner with an email and no namesakes lands at level 3, not 4.\n\nI also added the `java.time.temporal.ChronoUnit` import and updated the method's Javadoc to describe the new 1\u20134 range and the tenure requirement.\n\nThe full test suite (`AcceptanceTest`) passes: **BUILD SUCCESS, Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0**.",
