        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe tenure factor is added to the single method that already owns membership-level computation, so the logic lives in the right unit \u2014 no new catch-all, no misplaced responsibility. It extends the existing additive pattern cleanly:\n\n- Reuses the established `boolean <name>` + `if (...) level++;` idiom (`hasEmail`, `unique`, now `tenured`), so a maintainer reads it the same way as the lines above it.\n- The pre-tenure cap at 3 and the final cap at 4 are expressed with the same `Math.min` style already in use, making the two-stage capping explicit rather than duplicating or obscuring it.\n- Null-guards `registrationDate` consistently with the rest of the class (see `getRegistrationStatus` at line 160), and `ChronoUnit`/`LocalDate.now()` are the natural idioms here.\n- No duplication: the day-count comparison exists only once, and the Javadoc is updated to match the new 1\u20134 range and the never-exceeds-3-when-new invariant from the spec.\n\nThe method is still short and single-purpose; nothing here needs restructuring."
